Jahshaka patch 0031 -- a diffuse decal on a material whose Fresnel is a SCALAR
loses the WHOLE PBS shader: `pixelData.F0.xyz` where F0 is a float.

UPSTREAM BUG, and reachable in Studio long before any patch of ours: it needs a
diffuse decal and an ordinary authored F0, nothing else. Found by
`gi.probe_gate` on 2026-09-13 (lane-probevis), which was logging eight of these
per run while passing:

    ERROR: 0:1553: 'xyz' : vector swizzle selection out of range
    ERROR: 0:1553: '' : compilation terminated
    Fragment Program 100000020PixelShader_ps failed to compile.

THE CAUSE. `pixelData.F0` is of type `float_fresnel`, which is `midf3` only when
`fresnel_scalar` is set and `midf` otherwise -- upstream's own FresnelSwizzle
pair decides both (Main/500.Structs_piece_vs_piece_ps.any:283-287, and every
other write goes through `@insertpiece( FresnelSwizzle )`). The decal piece's
second branch runs for `metallic_workflow || fresnel_workflow || fresnel_scalar`
and writes `pixelData.F0.xyz` unconditionally. Of those three, the middle one --
an authored F0 in the NON-separate form, which is what
`HlmsPbsDatablock::setFresnel` writes for an ordinary material -- leaves F0
SCALAR, and `.xyz` on a float is a swizzle out of range. On Vulkan that means
`VulkanProgram::compile` throws and the permutation is gone.

A PERMUTATION THAT DOES NOT COMPILE RENDERS BLACK, SILENTLY. Measured on the
pristine pin, same binary, this hunk apart: the decal region of a panel whose
material carries a non-separate F0 reads r 0.000 g 0.000 b 0.000 where it should
reflect the room, and the suite's Ogre log carries 50 compile errors; with the
hunk, r 0.071 g 0.012 b 0.012 -- the red wall behind the camera -- and zero.

THE FIX is upstream's own idiom: split the assignment on `fresnel_scalar`, the
property that decides the type. `decalF0` stays a midf3 either way, so the
scalar branch takes its red channel, which is the same component
`HlmsPbsDatablock` writes into `material.F0.x` for a non-separate Fresnel.

WHY IT IS NOT PART OF 0028, which found it: 0028 gates the per-pixel probe loop
on a material's reflectance and excludes materials under a diffuse decal, so a
Jahshaka scene with decals generates this permutation far more often -- but the
bug is upstream's, needs no probe, no grid and no gate, and belongs in its own
patch so a tree that already carries 0028 applies one NEW patch instead of
resetting the file.

MEDIA-only (one Hlms .any template, CRLF -- edited in binary mode). Studio stages
media from the SOURCE tree, so every tree needs the patch loop / build-ogre.sh
rerun; no C++ is rebuilt by it.

Covered by tests/gi/test_gi_probe_gate.cpp: case (h) asserts the decal pixel is a
reflection rather than black, and case (i) greps the suite's own Ogre log and
asserts ZERO shader compile errors across every case it renders.
diff --git a/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/ForwardPlus_DecalsCubemaps_piece_ps.any b/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/ForwardPlus_DecalsCubemaps_piece_ps.any
